  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055663",
    "id": "q-51076",
    "status": "supported",
    "reason": null,
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-51076",
      "knowledge_point_id": "903cd6d7-18f2-5b53-a8e9-9aaef5589549",
      "knowledge_point": "Using the Trapezoidal Rule: Word Problem",
      "problem": "The following table shows the rate $r(t),$ in centimeters per hour, at which rain is falling during a two-hour period of a certain day.\n\n| $t\\,\\text{(hours)}$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $r\\,\\text{(centimeters/hour)}$ | $3$ | $4$ | $3$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nApproximate the total amount of rainfall during this period using the trapezoidal rule with $4$ trapezoids of equal height.",
      "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=r(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ represents the total amount of rainfall during the two-hour period.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(a)+2(r({t}_{1})+r({t}_{2})+⋯+r({t}_{n-1}))+r(b)]Δt,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δt=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=4.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,2],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-0}{4}=0.5.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(0)+2(r(0.5)+r(1)+r(1.5))+r(2)]\\cdot 0.5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table in the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1}{2}[3+2(4+3+3)+1]\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =0.25(24) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, approximately $6\\,\\text{cm}$ of rain fell during the given two-hour period.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
